---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<Base title="About Mural Marker">
  <PageLayout>
    <div class="p-4 lg:w-7/10 lg:mr-auto lg:ml-auto">
      <h3 class="text-2xl mb-2">About Mural Marker</h3>
      <p>
        Washington D.C. is home to a thriving community of artists and much of
        that creative expression finds its way onto the many walls of the city.
        But murals are temporary, and once they're painted over, they disappear
        forever. I wanted to create a tool that would archive these works while
        simultaneously providing a snapshot in time of the mural landscape. A
        more direct way of imagining how all of the works blended together. This
        is an incomplete record, and likely always will be, but hopefully piece
        by piece we can put together a more comprehensive picture of the city's
        art history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Have feedback or interested in helping out? Send a message to <a
          href="mailto:contact.muralmarker@gmail.com"
          >contact.muralmarker@gmail.com</a
        > and I'll get back to you as soon as possible!
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-2xl mt-4 mb-2">About Licensing &amp; Rights</h3>
      <p>
        The material on this site sits in a few different layers, and each one
        carries its own rights.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>
            <strong>Original content:</strong> The writing, mural locations, and other
            descriptive information I've compiled here are licensed under a <a
              href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
              rel="license noopener"
              target="_blank"
              >Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license</a
            >. Feel free to use it, adapt it, build on it, just credit Mural
            Marker and link back.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <strong>The Murals:</strong> The murals remain the copyright of the artists
            who created them. Nothing on this site grants any rights to reproduce,
            adapt, or commercially use the artwork. They are documented here for archival
            and educational purposes; if you want to use an image of a work, please
            contact the artist.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <strong>The Photographs:</strong> Photographs carry their own copyright
            held by the photographer. Because a photograph of a mural also depicts
            the underlying artwork, reusing one may require permission from both the
            photographer and the artist.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2">
        I've done my best to credit artists and photographers accurately, but
        records are incomplete and attributions are sometimes uncertain. If
        you're an artist or photographer and something here is miscredited, or
        you'd like your work removed, please write to <a
          href="mailto:contact.muralmarker@gmail.com"
          >contact.muralmarker@gmail.com</a
        > and I'll correct or take it down promptly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </PageLayout>
</Base>
